es":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6 stable.mono, haven't tested any other verison \n- Tested all 3 rendering backends and happens so probably an editor thing idk\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.stable.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - AMD Radeon RX 9070 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21030.31) - AMD Ryzen 9 5950X 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 95.92 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nin the scene tree dock when you expand and collapse a parent node fast enough you get:  \n\nERROR: editor/docks/scene_tree_dock.cpp:4202 - Parameter \"node\" is null.\n\nbut this only happens on expansion AND if any node in the scene tree isn't selected eg. the Inspector is empty\n\nThis doesn't interfere with editor function as far as I can tell, functionally my game stuff still works and the tree still collapses and expands properly.\n\nIf I collapse and expand the node tree slowly the error doesn't appear so might be a thread thing causing a race condition causing the state of filter_quick_menu = nullptr, but I didn't feel like following the call stack ¯\\\\__(ツ)__/¯\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- create a new project\n- create a scene root node\n- child any node to the scene root\n- click off a node to make sure the inspector is empty\n- collapse and expand the root scene node a few times quickly\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.githu